    {
      "id": "epf5tt8",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "LOCAL GOVERNMENT IN INDIA"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Panchayati Raj System follows a three-tier structure: Gram Panchayat at the village level, Panchayat Samiti at the block level, and Zila Parishad at the district level.",
        "The 73rd Constitutional Amendment Act, 1992 granted constitutional status to rural local self-governments, adding Part IX and the Eleventh Schedule.",
        "The 74th Constitutional Amendment Act, 1992 accorded constitutional recognition to urban local bodies, introducing Part IX-A and the Twelfth Schedule.",
        "Gram Sabha serves as the foundation of the Panchayati Raj system, comprising all adult registered voters within the Gram Panchayat area.",
        "Mandatory provisions include 5-year tenure for local bodies and reservation of seats for SCs, STs, and women."
      ],
      "id": "5wlxh87"
    },
